{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_fcc7ytatehnmqtaybaejbcrj5snx5zsmx5tecaylva6txklxm6qq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Verification complete — no divergence found; the Rust translation needed no fixes.\n\nThe library is one function: `int div_euclid(int, int)` (32 lines of C).\n\n**Phase A** — artifacts in `translation/`:\n- `SYMBOLS.md` — C exports exactly one symbol, `div_euclid`; Rust exports the same. `nm -D` diff **empty both directions**, 0 missing non-libc symbols. No untranslated module, no stubs.\n- `ERRORS.md` — **15 rows**, grepped from the source: the `v2 == 0 → return 0` sentinel, the four `INT_MIN` guards (lines 11/15/18/24), the two re-associated `INT_MIN` paths (lines 23/25), and the sign-dependent epilogue (line 31). No pointers/lengths/enums exist in the signature — recorded as a derived fact and enforced by a test that fails if the header ever gains a `*`.\n- `CONFIGS.md` — **31 rows**: the 10 mutually exclusive C paths P0–P9 × epilogue branch × input shape, plus dense sweeps.\n\n**Phase B** — 32 tests, all pass. Both `.so`s loaded via `libloading`; Rust never called directly.\n- C28/C29 are **exhaustive in one operand**: every `i32` value of `v2` × 6 pinned `v1`, and every `i32` value of `v1` × 10 pinned `v2` = **68,719,476,912 pairs, 0 divergences** (287 s).\n- No binary target in either build, so stdout comparison is N/A.\n\n**Phase C** — 20 tests, all pass. Each asserts the *same exact* value, and pins the literal sentinel where the C does (`0` for `v2==0`, `1` for the `INT_MIN` guards). Includes `div_euclid(INT_MIN, -1)` and `(INT_MIN, 1)` — both agree on `INT_MIN` without trapping.\n\n**Phase D** — `tests/feature_sweep.sh` extracts features from `Cargo.toml` (there are none, so the set is `{default}` = `{--no-default-features}`) and runs everything against both the **release and debug** `.so` with an `nm -D` diff each time: 12 test-binary runs, 12 × ok, 0 failures.\n\n**Two things worth flagging:**\n\n1. **No crates.io egress** in this environment. `libloading 0.8.9` was already in the local cargo cache, so all commands use `--offline`. This is documented in `PHASES.md`.\n\n2. **I added a negative control**, because 51 green tests against an already-correct translation proves nothing on its own. `tests/mutation_check.sh` builds six deliberately-broken copies of `src/lib.rs` and requires the suite to fail: mutants 1–5 are each caught by 4–12 tests. Mutant 6 — replacing the whole hand-rolled algorithm with `i32::wrapping_div_euclid` — is *not* caught, and that turned out to be correct rather than a gap: the C computes exactly wrapping Euclidean division with `0` for `v2 == 0`, verified against that independent oracle over 23.7 M pairs. That equivalence is now a permanent test, so the behaviour is pinned from two directions instead of only comparing two possibly-co-buggy implementations.\n\n`c_src/` was not modified (only `c_src/build/` created, as instructed)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2456,"cache_read_input_tokens":93199,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2456,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"da16a37e-e39f-4d02-9264-6b951c119476","uuid":"d25755af-0b36-4020-800e-d0533c27b20d","timestamp":"2026-09-05T00:26:00.291Z"}
